/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A solenoid is a coil with a movable iron plunger.
   - F is force in newtons (N); μ0 = 4π×10⁻⁷ H/m; N is coil turns; I is coil current in A; A is pole face area in m²; g is air gap in m.
   - At switch-on the air gap is large, so the solenoid needs a pull-in current.
   - Iavg ≈ D Vb / Rc
   - Iavg is average coil current in A; D is duty cycle from 0 to 1; Vb is battery voltage in V; Rc is coil resistance in Ω.
   - A low-side driver switches the coil's ground side with a MOSFET (metal-oxide-semiconductor field-effect transistor); a high-side driver switches the battery side.
   - A relay is an electromagnetic switch.
   - An H-bridge drives a DC motor in both directions.
   - A stepper motor moves in fixed angular steps.
   - β is the step angle in degrees and S is the number of steps per revolution.
*/
