/* book: lead: A fluid-mechanical actuator uses a fluid under pressure, oil (hydraulic) or air and vacuum (pneumatic), to make a force or a movement. The ECU does not push the load itself: it drives a small solenoid valve that lets pressure into a cylinder or onto a diaphragm, and the fluid does the heavy work. This is how a turbo wastegate opens, an automatic gearbox engages a clutch, an ABS unit lowers brake p */
