/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Every fluid actuator turns fluid energy into mechanical work with the same three relations.
   - F is force in N; Δp is the pressure difference across the piston in Pa; A is the effective area in m²; v is piston speed in m/s; Q is volume flow in m³/s; P is power in W.
   - The pressure source differs.
   - The interface between the ECU and the fluid is a valve worked by a solenoid.
   - Because the valve only meters a small flow, a 1 A solenoid can command kilonewtons of clamping force.
   - A diaphragm actuator has a rubber diaphragm in a pressed-steel can with a return spring.
*/
