/* book exam traps: Use the pressure difference across the piston, and in pascals: 1 bar = 10⁵ Pa and 1 kPa = 1000 Pa. Boost read as 0.6 bar is 60 000 Pa, not 0.6 Pa. | For an annular (ring) piston the area is π(D² − d²) ÷ 4, not π(D − d)² ÷ 4. | A diaphragm actuator does not move until the pressure force exceeds the spring preload; below that it stays shut. | A PWM valve does not give a pressure proportional to duty in a straight line; the ECU uses a map or closes the loop with a pressure sensor. | Hydraulic and pneumatic are not interchangeable words: oil hardly compresses (stiff, holds position), air compresses (soft, needs a spring to set position). */
